    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": ". However, most often, the real-time dataset is read diagonally, since this allows to build time series of revisions on which the descriptive analysis is carried out. For example, the main diagonal (in red) collects all the data series when it was first released, the first sub-diagonal (in orange) collects all the data series after it was revised once, and so on.",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "As an example, the file below reports a revision triangle of the GDP series, and it has been published to demonstrate the reliability of the GDP estimates for the Euro area. The reported revision triangle is relative to the period 2017:Q4-2020:Q3. In particular, this example shows an application to the Quarter on Quarter percentage rates of changes of seasonally and calendar adjusted GDP.",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
