  "突き合わせ・推定": [
   {
    "quote": "Given a particular indicator (that is, a time series) and two subsequent estimates of it, which both refer to the same period",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "is a a preliminary (or earlier) estimate and",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "a later (more recent) estimate of the indicator. This definition of revision is used when dealing with indicators measured in growth rates (period-on-period or year-on-year growth rates). Instead, when dealing with revisions to values in level, we define revisions in relative terms:",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "represents the point in time when the vintage that contained that particular estimate of the indicator was released, that is, when the indicator relative to time",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "was estimated. The real-time dataset is constructed as follows.",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": ", from the preliminary estimates to the latest (such information is useful to assess the reliability of the earlier estimates). Finally, when triangles are read along the main diagonal (or the first sub-diagonal, or the second sub-diagonal, …), they give the time series of the first (or second, or third, …) releases. To be more specific, assuming that",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "is the preliminary estimate of the indicator relative to time",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "It is easy to understand why it is called triangle, since the grey part of the table represents forecasts and not data that is actually available at the moment of its release. The first column collects the subsequent revisions that have been made to update the estimate of the indicator relative to time",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "The sign of this measure indicates wether on average the estimate of the earlier releases is biased. This bias is positive (negative) if the sign of the statistics is negative (positive). However, since revisions of opposite sign cancel out, this measure, often also called “average bias”, is of limited use.",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "A modified t-test can be performed to determine whether the mean revision is statistically different from zero, which may give an insight on wether an actual bias exists in the preliminary estimates. The t statistics is computed as",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Correlation between revision and earlier estimate (test if revisions are “noise”).",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "is statistically significant, this implies that there was information available at the time of the first estimate which was not efficiently exploited and therefore the revisions can be interpreted as “noise”.",
    "url": "https://aciancetta.github.io/Euorostat-EMOS-TimeSeries/revisions-analysis.html",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Correlation between revision and earlier estimate (test if revisions are “news”).",
